WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.380
Post with a plan, stay safe, and measure what works.

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:08.570
This is the video for module three of Personal Branding and Online Presence.

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:20.920
Content pillars are the three or four main topics you post about again and again. Without them, posting becomes random, and random posting confuses people about what you do.

4
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.210
Here are four kinds that work for most people. Imagine a caterer.

5
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.280
Teach: how to keep jollof from burning at the bottom of a big pot.

6
00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:35.750
Show the work: a video of 200 packs being prepared for a wedding.

7
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.200
Proof: a client's thank-you message, shared with permission.

8
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:45.060
Personal: why she started catering after her mother's canteen.

9
00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:57.870
For example, Ngozi is a makeup artist in Owerri with about 3 hours a week for content. Her pillars are skin prep tips, bridal looks, client reviews and her training journey.

10
00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:03.920
Her rhythm is 2 Instagram posts and 4 WhatsApp Status updates a week.

11
00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:15.310
Every Sunday, on Wi-Fi to save data, she spends 2 hours editing photos, writing captions in her notes app and recording one 30-second tip video.

12
00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.630
She posts on Tuesday and Friday, and her Status uses cuts from the same material.

13
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:32.700
Then 10 minutes a day replying to comments. Posting twice a week for six months builds more trust than posting every day for two weeks and then vanishing.

14
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:39.370
Start with a hook. For example: most bridal makeup cracks by evening for one reason.

15
00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:45.270
Then give two to five short lines that teach, show or prove something specific.

16
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.610
Add a clear photo or short video of your real work.

17
00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:56.210
And end with a next step, such as save this, or book with the WhatsApp link in my bio.

18
00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:05.040
Your goal is to be easy to find for work, and hard to target for harm. Here are three scams that target public profiles.

19
00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:15.780
Code theft. A message, often from a friend's hacked account, asks you to forward a code sent by mistake. It is your login code. Never share it.

20
00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:28.470
Impersonation. Someone copies your name and photo and asks your customers for payment. Warn customers on Status that you only use one number, and report the fake account.

21
00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:35.690
Fake payment alerts. Always confirm the money in your own bank or wallet app before you deliver.

22
00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:45.280
A client's name, face, house, chat or result belongs to her. Posting them without asking can embarrass her and break her trust.

23
00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:59.690
For example, Bisi is an interior decorator in Ibadan. A happy client sent photos of her finished living room. Bisi asked in writing if she could share two photos and one line from her message.

24
00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:11.030
The client agreed, but asked that her name is not used. Bisi cropped out a family portrait and a window showing the street, and saved the permission in a folder called Permissions.

25
00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:24.380
Before you post, check five things. No home address or routine. No children's school details. No ID or card numbers. Client permission obtained. And every claim is true.

26
00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:39.210
Nigeria has the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023. For a small business, that means collect only the customer data you need, keep it secure, and never add people to broadcast lists without their agreement.

27
00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:48.800
How do you know your brand is working? By what happens because of it. Every time someone new contacts you, ask politely how they heard about you.

28
00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:55.430
Write it in a simple enquiry log: the date, the source, what they wanted, and the result.

29
00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:10.520
For example, Halima, the Kano bookkeeper, had 7 new enquiries in her first month. 3 became paying clients, all from WhatsApp Status and referrals. Her Instagram tips got saves, but no enquiries.

30
00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:22.590
So she kept Status at 4 updates a week and added a clear booking line to her Instagram tips. Give any change at least four weeks before you judge it, and never buy followers.

31
00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:37.220
Your practice. Choose three or four pillars and a weekly rhythm you can keep. Batch your first four posts in one sitting. Review your WhatsApp privacy settings. Then start your enquiry log and your Permissions folder.

32
00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:39.720
Now continue with the lessons below.
